cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or data, please cite it as below and also cite the upstream sources (see DATA_LICENSE.md)."
title: "Türkiye Bitki DNA Barkod Atlası (Turkey Plant DNA Barcode Atlas)"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Karadağ"
    given-names: "Arda"
  - family-names: "Menekşe"
    given-names: "Buse"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ArdaKaradag36/bioatlastr"
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-11-04"
version: "0.2.0"
keywords: [DNA barcoding, rbcL, matK, ITS, Turkey, flora, plants]
abstract: "A research atlas that asks whether short DNA barcode regions (rbcL, matK, ITS) can separate the vascular plant species of Turkey. Species names come from WCVP (Kew); sequences come from ENA/INSDC. Success is measured with a threshold-free nearest-neighbour test: every evaluated sequence of a species must match its own species. BOLD was not searched. Results are estimates without expert verification and must not be used for scientific, regulatory or commercial decisions."
